  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Brexpiprazole may be associated with Anxiety Disorder through a series of indirect pathways. The drug is indicated for Major Depressive Disorder, and this indication is linked to two other conditions—Gepirone and Levomilnacipran—both of which are indicated for Anxiety Disorder. Similarly, Reboxetine, another condition linked to Anxiety Disorder, is also indicated for Major Depressive Disorder. This suggests that Brexpiprazole may exert a modulatory effect on the pathophysiology of anxiety through its role in treating depression. The scores, which reflect the strength of the relationships, are consistent across the three paths, indicating a potential for Brexpiprazole to be considered a candidate for repositioning in the treatment of Anxiety Disorder. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Brexpiprazole and anxiety, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
